    "severity": {
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "coolant-loss-is-one-of-the-most-serious-warning-signs",
          "title": "Coolant loss is one of the most serious warning signs",
          "description": "Coolant loss is one of the most serious warning signs you can ignore. It's the primary cause of engine overheating - and overheating destroys engines.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "In our 24,650 quote dataset, we identified four primary causes:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "External leak (45% of cases) - Hoses, radiator, water pump. Repair: £50-£700.",
                "Head gasket failure (30% of cases) - Coolant entering combustion chamber. Repair: £550-£2,000+.",
                "Internal leak (15% of cases) - Cracked head or block. Repair: £1,000-£3,000+.",
                "Heater matrix leak (10% of cases) - Coolant leak inside cabin. Repair: £300-£800."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The critical rule: If your temperature gauge enters the red zone, you have minutes - not hours - to stop the engine. Continuing to drive will warp the cylinder head, crack the block, and seize the engine."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Common affected vehicles & engines"
            }
          ],
          "links": [],
          "source": {
            "sectionId": "coolant-loss-is-one-of-the-most-serious-warning-signs",
            "order": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "don-t-fall-for-these-common-misconceptions",
          "title": "Don't fall for these common misconceptions",
          "description": "“I'll just top up the coolant and keep driving.”",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "You're masking the problem. Coolant loss always gets worse."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "“The temperature gauge is fine - it's not overheating.”"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Coolant loss can occur without immediate overheating. The damage accumulates."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "“It's just a hose - cheap fix.”"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Sometimes. But in 40% of cases, it's head gasket or internal - much more expensive."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "“I can use a stop-leak product.”"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Stop-leak products clog your cooling system and often make things worse. Proper repair is the only reliable solution."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Diagnostic flowchart"
            }
          ],
          "links": [],
          "source": {
            "sectionId": "don-t-fall-for-these-common-misconceptions",
            "order": 3
          }
        }
      ]
    },
